course: dictionary
lesson: 3400
title: Expire: when time runs out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The verb expire usually means that something stops being valid or usable after a set time. «My bus ticket has expired» means I can no longer use it.
explain: Food and medicine can expire too. «The milk has expired» means it is past the date when it is safe or best to use. Look for the «use by» or expiry date on the label to check.
explain: In old or formal English, expire can mean to die. You will meet this in old stories and official writing. Check the clues around it: a serious tone, or a character who is very old or ill. Then try the everyday meaning in the sentence. If it does not make sense, the other meaning is probably right.
fact: Expire is a verb: expire, expires, expired, expiring.
fact: When something expires, it stops being valid or usable after a certain time.
fact: Tickets, passports, library loans, coupons and passwords can all expire.
fact: Food or medicine that has expired is past the date when it is safe or best to use.
fact: In old or formal English, «expire» can mean to die. Context tells you which meaning is used.
exercise: «My bus ticket has expired, so I cannot use it.» What does expired mean here? | It has been found in the lost property | It is now cheaper | *It is no longer valid after its time | It has been pressed flat in a book
exercise: Mum says, «Do not eat that yogurt, the date has expired.» What does she mean? | It has just been bought from the shop | It is cold and fresh from the fridge | *It is past the date when it is safe to eat
exercise: In an old story, the narrator says, «The old king expired in his sleep.» What does expired mean here? | *Died | Got married | Went out to the garden | Woke up
test: Which sentence uses expire in the everyday sense of stopping being valid? | «The cat will expire on the sofa.» | «The river will expire into the sea.» | *«Your library loan will expire next Friday.» | «The sun will expire over the hill.»
test: What is an expiry date? | The date when a shop opens | *The date after which something is no longer valid or safe to use | The date when a film is released | The date of a birthday party
exam: Why do you check the «use by» date on food? | To see how much it costs | To find out who made it | *To know when the food stops being safe to eat | To see which shelf to put it on
